  "answer": "Project Zenith, an initiative by Zenith Aerospace Inc., is currently in its development phase following the successful completion of the design phase, with lead developer Omar Jensen providing guidance. The project has secured a $2M budget approved by the executive board to cover research, development, and marketing, with detailed allocations to be discussed on August 1st. Additionally, a $15,000 training budget has been approved for the coding team and project managers, with sessions starting next month. To support these efforts, the team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, including Mike Chen and Lisa Ray. Strategic partnerships have been established with TechInnovate, an AI research leader, to leverage AI in enhancing data visualization tools. The team is currently gathering innovative proposals from R&D by July 20th and seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience by the end of November. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, will be updated effective January next year. An onboarding session for new team members is scheduled for September 10th."
